INTERPRETATION
  1/w is a CENTRAL-PATH coordinate. w=inf = analytic center Plat(C).
  Peeling far runners one at a time = following the central path inward.
  A Beurling-Selberg minorant proves the CENTER (bounded core, finite) is positive;
  the far runner is the barrier whose 1/w residual is a SIGNED but BOUNDED Dedekind
  sum -- exactly the signed content that positivity-only methods miss, now isolated
  to a finite periodic object instead of the divergent |T|>=3 absolute tail.
